  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Invest Integra Partners</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This partnership was launched under USAIDs Digital Invest program, a partnership initiative between USAIDs Innovation, Technology, and Research Hub, the Gender Equality &amp; Women&apos;s Empowerment Hub (GenDev), and the State Department, under the U.S. Digital Connectivity and Cybersecurity Partnership (DCCP). The Digital Invest program has two objectives: 1) Support the sustainable growth and expansion of competitive internet service providers (ISPs) in emerging markets, and 2) Support the sustainable growth and expansion of competitive financial technology companies in emerging markets. Integra Partners is an impact focused venture capital fund manager that makes investments in early-stage technology companies across Southeast Asia, with a secondary focus on South Asia. Integras mission is to drive impact and inclusion in Southeast Asia across financial services, insurance, and digital health with an aim to give every person and business in the region the ability to manage and improve their financial and physical health digitally and at a reasonable cost.</narrative>
  </description>
